  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM - Multi-country humanitarian assistance &#x2013; 2025/26</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the conflict began on April 15, 2023, over 1.1 million people have crossed into South Sudan, with 72 per cent being South Sudanese returnees. Many arrive exhausted and stranded in remote border areas, requiring onward transportation assistance (OTA). Through this funding, the International Organization for Migration provides life-saving support through movement assistance to nearly 4,000 stranded and vulnerable returnees affected by the Sudan crisis. This assistance mitigates the physical, health and protection risks associated with displacement, ensuring that conflict-affected individuals experience safe and dignified human mobility.</narrative>
  </description>
